 "result": "{\"answer\": \"35 states. Congress sent the ERA to the states on 22 March 1972 with a seven-year ratification deadline of 22 March 1979. By that date 35 of the required 38 states (three-fourths of the 50 states) had ratified it \u2014 leaving it three short. (Complicating matters, five of those states \u2014 Nebraska, Tennessee, Idaho, Kentucky and South Dakota \u2014 had passed measures purporting to rescind their ratifications, though the validity of such rescissions is legally disputed.) Congress subsequently extended the deadline to 30 June 1982, but no additional states ratified during the extension; Nevada (2017), Illinois (2018) and Virginia (2020) ratified long afterward, raising the total to 38, though the legal effect of those late ratifications remains contested.\", \"confidence\": \"high\", \"abstained\": false}",
